## 2. Install the AWS CLI tool
The file you downloaded is only 134 bytes, which means you downloaded an error page or a XML redirect, not the actual AWS CLI installer. The URL you used is incorrect.
## 🛠️ The Fix
The correct download URL requires awscli.amazonaws.com. Run these commands in your terminal to download and install the official AWS CLI: [1, 2] 

# 1. Download the correct zip file
curl "https://awscli.amazonaws.com/awscli-exe-linux-x86_64.zip" -o "awscliv2.zip"
# 2. Unzip the installer
unzip awscliv2.zip
# 3. Run the installation script
sudo ./aws/install

## 🔍 Why it failed
The address amazonaws.com is a root domain for AWS services, not the hosting location for the CLI tool. Because the URL didn't point to a real file, the server returned a tiny text-based error message (134 bytes) and saved it as a .zip file. [3, 4] 
If you run into issues with the unzip command, let me know if you get a "command not found" error or an "end of central directory signature not found" error so we can fix it.

## 3. Verify the installation
Check if the tool was installed correctly by printing its version number: [6] 

aws --version

If you see an output like aws-cli/1.x.x or aws-cli/2.x.x, the installation was successful.
